---
title: Pulsar starting recipe by Scott Rao
source: https://www.scottrao.com/blog/pulsar-recipe
---

@Pulsar 25g 425g 100°C -- just off the boil
grind medium -- coarser than for a hand pour, about 800 µm

/rinse -- wet the filter with the valve open, then drain
/level-bed -- shake the Pulsar, or stir with a WDT tool
0:00 75g bloom
0:00 /close
0:45 /open -- after filling to 1 cm above the grounds
0:45 425g pulse -- several short pours, keep the slurry 1-2 cm high
/swirl -- gently, after the last pour

target 4:00 -- 3:30 to 4:30: grind finer if faster, coarser if slower
